From: mocha device tree
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: guard notifyBarPanelExpansionChanged against a null bar

KeyguardViewMediator can ask for the notification panel to expand before
StatusBar has finished building its view, so PanelView.mBar -- set by
setBar() from makeStatusBarView() -- is still null:

  FATAL EXCEPTION: main (com.android.systemui)
  java.lang.NullPointerException: Attempt to invoke virtual method
    'void PanelBar.panelExpansionChanged(float, boolean)' on a null object
    at PanelView.notifyBarPanelExpansionChanged(PanelView.java:1173)
    at PanelView.expand(PanelView.java:1002)
    at StatusBar.instantExpandNotificationsPanel(StatusBar.java:5177)
    at StatusBar.updatePanelExpansionForKeyguard(StatusBar.java:4696)
    at StatusBarKeyguardViewManager.showBouncerOrKeyguard(...:183)
    at KeyguardViewMediator.handleShow(KeyguardViewMediator.java:1772)

On mocha this reproduces on every boot that reaches the lock screen, and
SystemUI restarts in a loop, so the device comes up with no UI at all.

Guard in notifyBarPanelExpansionChanged() rather than at the StatusBar call
site: every caller reaches the bar through this one method, and there is
nothing meaningful to notify before the bar exists -- the expansion state is
pushed again once setBar() has run.

The hunk deliberately carries no blank context lines: several editors strip
the leading space from them and git then rejects the patch as corrupt.

--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/phone/PanelView.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/phone/PanelView.java
@@ -1172,5 +1172,11 @@
     protected void notifyBarPanelExpansionChanged() {
+        // The keyguard can ask the panel to expand before StatusBar has built
+        // its view and called setBar(). Nothing to report yet in that case;
+        // the state is pushed again once the bar is attached.
+        if (mBar == null) {
+            return;
+        }
         mBar.panelExpansionChanged(mExpandedFraction, mExpandedFraction > 0f
                 || mPeekAnimator != null || mInstantExpanding || isPanelVisibleBecauseOfHeadsUp()
                 || mTracking || mHeightAnimator != null);
     }
